= Preprint — Simple =

A preprint is a complete public draft of a scholarly or scientific work made available before it has been certified by a journal or conference peer-review process.

Preprints can accelerate dissemination, establish priority, invite feedback, and expose work to wider scrutiny. Authors may revise them, submit them for formal publication, or leave them without a later peer-reviewed version.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* preprint ≠ peer-reviewed article
* public availability ≠ peer-review certification

